plain java
--------\
int[] arr = {1, 2, 4, 5, 6};

int n = 6;

int expectedSum = n * (n + 1) / 2;

int actualSum = 0;

for (int num : arr) {
    actualSum += num;
}

System.out.println(expectedSum - actualSum);

java 8
---------
int[] arr = {1, 2, 4, 5, 6};

int n = 6;

int actualSum = Arrays.stream(arr).sum();

int expectedSum = IntStream.rangeClosed(1, n).sum();

System.out.println(expectedSum - actualSum);

D. Complexity
Solution	Time	Extra space
Plain Java	O(n)	O(1)
Java 8	O(n)	O(1) auxiliary space

E. Choice of solution
Both approaches are efficient.

Use the mathematical formula when the input constraints are clear.

For very large integer ranges, consider long to prevent integer overflow.


